__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
**/.reticuli/tmp/
**/.reticuli/draft.jsonl
# An audit receipt is one machine's momentary re-earn -- true for its host and
# minute, read locally by `ret status`, and not a root input. Tracking it only
# committed a value that went stale the next time anyone audited anywhere. The
# seal (manifest.json, parts.json) stays tracked; the receipt does not.
**/.reticuli/audit.json
# assess leaves the same kind of residue: one machine's measurements, stamped
# with the root they were taken against and read back by `ret status --all`.
# Local evidence, not repository content, and never a root input.
**/.reticuli/assess.json
.checkwork/
.launcher/
.selfclaim/
build/
dist/
examples/make/wordcount
# Residue: a claim's working output, not its identity. These patterns need
# the ** prefix -- a gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to the
# directory the file sits in, so `.reticuli/mutation_score.json` matched only
# the repo root and let a nested one be committed inside a sealed claim.
**/.reticuli/mutation_score.json

# Layer verdicts dropped in the repository root. Each suite writes its verdict
# when it finds a claim.toml beside it -- "am I running as a claim's gate?" --
# and that became true at the root the moment the repository sealed itself. The
# guard is too coarse: a claim.toml being present is not the same as THIS suite
# being that claim's gate. REPO_OK is not here: it is the root claim's own
# pinned output and belongs in the tree.
/AGENTS_OK
/AUTHORING_OK
/EXCHANGE_OK
/KERNEL_OK
/LAUNCHER_OK
/SURFACE_OK
# the decomposed kernel sub-claim verdicts
/CORE_OK
/RECIPE_OK
/IDENTITY_OK
/SEAL_OK
/RUN_OK
/BUILD_OK
/ATTEST_OK
# the decomposed surface sub-claim verdicts
/MEASURE_OK
/BASE_OK
/RENDER_OK
/HANDLERS_OK
/PARSER_OK
/VERBS_OK

# local research notes, never committed
deep-research.md
deep-repo-struct.md
